  "description": "meme-id: i_am_not_racist_some_of_my_best_slaves_are_black; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a close-up of black ants carrying what appear to be larvae or pupae, juxtaposed with the text 'i am not racist some of my best slaves are black.' This creates a harmful and hateful analogy that equates Black people with enslaved Africans and uses the visual of ants (often stereotyped as primitive or animal-like) to reinforce racist tropes. The meme leverages the visual of ants to imply that Black people are inherently inferior or suited for servitude, directly invoking anti-Black racism and the historical legacy of slavery. The intent is to normalize or justify racial prejudice by using a dehumanizing metaphor, which is a form of hateful content targeting Black people based on race.",
